# text = This is what I had to say ; and what I say , I mean to do Uncle Mas'r Davy I'll go in now , Trot and look after Little Blossom , who will be getting up presently Not along of my being heer , ma'am , I hope Unless my wits is gone a bahd's neezing ' - by which Mr . Peggotty meant to say , bird's-nesting - ' this morning , 'tis along of me as you're a-going to quit us You have something to say , my good friend and will do better without me By your leave , ma'am I should take it kind , pervising you doen't mind my clicketten , if you'd bide heer Would you Then I am sure I will I took my dear child away last night to my lodging , wheer I have a long time been expecting of her and preparing fur her .
